- **Wildcard escaping:** `_` and `%` are `LIKE` wildcards, so I escape them in `domain`. Otherwise `find_users_by_domain(db, "a_b.com")` would also match `axb.com`.
- **Case sensitivity:** SQLite's `LIKE` is case-insensitive for ASCII by default, so `Example.COM` matches `example.com`.
- **Result order:** Like `search_users`, there is no `order by`, so which 50 rows you get isn't deterministic when more than 50 users match. Adding `order by created desc` would match `recent_users` if you want stable results.
